WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:16.840
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.010
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:26.200
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.860
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.700
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.160
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.800
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.190
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:52.280
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:57.530
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:03.309
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:09.020
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
Robert's Rebellion, also known as the War

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.500
of the Usurper, was a rebellion against House
Targaryen, primarily instigated by Eddard

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.590
Stark, Jon Arryn, and Robert Baratheon, for
whom it's named.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.039
It lasted "close to a year" and resulted in
the end of the Targaryen dynasty in the Seven

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:27.060
Kingdoms
and the beginning of Robert Baratheon's reign.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.470
The most important battle during this war
and the battle that ultimately determined

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:36.090
the outcome of Robert's Rebellion was the
Battle of the Trident. The battle was fought

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:41.060
between rebel and royal troops at the Trident,
across what would thereafter be known as the

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.780
ruby ford.
A legendary duel between Robert and Rhaegar

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:49.640
was a fight which decided the outcome of the
entire battle. The battle was decided when

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:55.400
Robert and Rhaegar met in single combat on
horseback in the stream. Robert eventually

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.810
crushed Rhaegar's chest with a blow of his
warhammer.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.990
This battle was the most important event during
the rebellion as it decided the winner of

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.880
the war.
However, all the circumstances and the entire

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.250
truth will not be known until the final seasons
of House of the Dragon end. What if there

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.690
are some secrets we don’t know yet regarding
this battle.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.960
As you may or may not know, Fire &amp; Blood book
on which the upcoming Game of Thrones prequel

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:25.129
is based on is not entirely accurate as it's
not written by George RR Martin's point of

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:30.439
view, but rather George writes it from Maester's
point of view who gathers his information

00:02:30.439 --> 00:02:35.079
from other history books and sources alike.
Also, the only characters who saw Rhaegar

00:02:35.079 --> 00:02:39.959
fall, saw only the final blow.
What if Robert did not win a fight against

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.400
Rhaegar or what if he did, but Rhaegar defeated
him.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:48.260
What if Prince Rhaegar defeated Robert and
told him to yield since he did not want to

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.150
kill him?
Rhaegar told him that Lyanna loves him and

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:57.209
he loves her. Robert yielded, Rhaegar helped
Robert get up and when Rhaegar wasn't ready,

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:02.549
when he put down his sword, at that moment
Robert smashed his warhammer into Prince Rhaegar's

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:08.099
chest. That’s why Robert was never happy.
He knew Lyanna loved Rhaegar and Rhaegar did

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:14.099
not hurt her. Robert knew Rhaegar was a better
fighter. He defeated Rhaegar only because

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:19.500
Rhaegar was too noble and kind to finish him
so Robert used the situation, yielded and

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:25.140
killed him when he was not expecting it. That's
why he drank himself to an early grave, trying

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.620
to forget it all. I mean, it's all there.
It's been in front of us for years: during

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.290
his battle against Rhaegar, Robert was wounded,
and after that battle, he was never truly

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:40.230
happy. Some say it's because of Lyanna, but
the truth is, Robert never really loved Lyanna

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.909
that much. As matter of fact, he slept with
many girls after his marriage was arranged

00:03:44.909 --> 00:03:49.439
to Lyanna. In this theory, the truth why Robert
was never happy again after the battle of

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:54.359
the Trident is not only because his betrothed
ran away with Rhaegar out of love and not

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:59.579
against her will, but also because that same
man Lyanna fell in love with, defeated him

00:03:59.579 --> 00:04:05.290
in combat and spared his life only for Robert
to kill him out of anger, even though he yielded

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:10.810
and Rhaegar was not expecting it. So basically,
in this theory, Robert knew Lyanna loved Rhaegar

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:15.579
and he loved her. Robert also knew Rhaegar
was a better fighter and he knows he would

00:04:15.579 --> 00:04:19.750
have been dead if not for Rhaegar's mercy
and that's why he's been drinking himself

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:25.480
to an early grave ever since. He couldn't
accept it. That’s why Robert dreams of Rhaegar

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:30.800
every night and kills him in his dreams every
night over and over again. It hunts him. That's

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.979
one theory and possibility. The other is that
Rhaegar was not even there, did not fight

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:41.690
Robert and did not die there. The story says
Prince Rhaegar met Lord Robert Baratheon in

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:47.060
combat at a ford during the Battle of the
Trident, where the pair had a legendary duel

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.430
in the raging rivers of the Trident. Rhaegar
despite wounding Robert, was struck down with

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:58.160
a massive blow from Robert's warhammer, which
scattered rubies encrusted in Rhaegar's armor

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:01.440
under the water.
It's said that "rubies flew like drops of

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.480
blood from the chest of a dying prince and
he sank to his knees in the water and with

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:11.490
his last breath murmured a woman's name".
While Rhaegar laid dead in the stream, soldiers

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:17.379
of both armies scrabbled in the water to search
for the rubies. Later the location was named

00:05:17.379 --> 00:05:22.569
the ruby ford. First let’s point out the
obvious - it's especially highlighted that

00:05:22.569 --> 00:05:27.340
Rhaegar wore his iconic night-black plate
armor with the three headed dragon of House

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:32.479
Targaryen decorated in rubies on its breastplate.
Additionally, the ford in which this battle

00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:36.770
took place is named for the rubies that were
knocked from Prince Rhaegar's breastplate.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:41.600
Now, why is it so important for George RR
Martin as well as for the showrunners to make

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.611
it very clear that Rhaegar wore his iconic
armor that had rubies attached to it. Why

00:05:46.611 --> 00:05:51.580
so much focus on Rhaegar's rubies? Why is
it such a big plot point and subject brought

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.110
up whenever the battle of the Trident or Rhaegar
are brought up? The first theory would be

00:05:56.110 --> 00:06:01.220
that Robert did not fight Rhaegar, but rather
someone else who had glamoured himself in

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:07.090
the form of Rhaegar using rubies. As it was
confirmed in the sixth season of Game of Thrones,

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:12.500
rubies can be used to glamor its owners into
a form or person they want to be. Melisandre

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:18.150
uses it to hide her true form of an extremely
old woman. In the books, Mance Rayder glamored

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:22.190
to appear as Rattleshirt via the ruby in his
wrist cuff.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.430
The power in rubies is something called glamor
where you can basically use them with the

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:31.990
power of the lord of light to project a different
image of yourself. If Melisandre and Mance

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.389
can use it,
it's most certainly not out of the realm of

00:06:34.389 --> 00:06:39.930
possibilities that someone had glamoured himself
in the form of Rhaegar using these same rubies

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:45.400
- and sacrificed his life for beloved Prince.
The other theory that is also supported says

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.979
that someone else died instead of Rhaegar
wearing his iconic armor. Remember that in

00:06:50.979 --> 00:06:55.540
the books because he'd been covered from head
to toe in armor, Dany did not see his face

00:06:55.540 --> 00:07:00.500
in the vision. Perhaps Rhaegar never died
on the Trident. While the first theory says

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:05.580
it was someone who used rubies to glamor himself
in the form of Rhaegar, the second one has

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:11.030
less magic and states it was simply one of
the kingsguard members who fought Robert,

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:15.919
dressed up in Rhaegar's full armor. Throughout
the books we've been given a few major examples

00:07:15.919 --> 00:07:20.970
of an ordinary fighter wearing his hero's
armor to sacrifice his life for him and his

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:26.449
cause. In a Clash of Kings, Ser Rodrik Cassel
attempted to put an end to Ramsay and his

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:32.740
atrocities. Rodrik's party comes across Ramsay
during one of his hunting trips, but Ramsey

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:37.300
is able to survive by switching clothes with
his personal servant who is then killed in

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:43.009
his place. Basically Ramsay gave him his clothes
and markings of identity whereupon Rodrik's

00:07:43.009 --> 00:07:47.740
men killed the servant believing him to be
Ramsay. Another example can be found in the

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:53.870
legendary last fight between Robar Royce (the
last of Bronze Kings) and Artys Arryn, the

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:59.990
founder of House Arryn. It says it was dusk
when Artys and his Andal army finally appeared.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:05.550
But even in that fading light, Robar Royce
did not fail to mark their leader. His silvered

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:11.250
armor and winged helm made the Falcon Knight
unmistakable, even from afar. After the first

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:16.960
6 charges against Robar's line failed, Artys's
falcon shaped helmet appeared in the heat

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:21.920
of the battle. Robar charged at him in the
hope that the Andal army would dissolve if

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.069
their leader was killed. There we had two
legendary heroes meeting and fighting in a

00:08:26.069 --> 00:08:31.710
duel except for a fact one of them was just
an ordinary knight. Robar beheaded the Falcon

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:37.510
Knight after a duel, only to see five hundred
fresh Andal knights charging at him with the

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:43.409
real Falcon Knight, Artys Arryn, at their
head. Cunning even more than brute force,

00:08:43.409 --> 00:08:49.450
Artys had clad one of his knights in his own
distinctive armor to distract Robar. Afterward,

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:54.070
Artys became King of the Mountain and the
Vale and founded house Arryn. Those are two

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:59.140
examples of someone else wearing their hero's
iconic armor to sacrifice his life for him

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:04.950
and his cause. There's definitely a reason
why George RR Martin is giving us these examples.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:10.230
There's also one detail from the popular episode
Blackwater that supports this theory. When

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:14.670
that episode had come out, George RR Martin
was pretty upset that main characters like

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:19.000
Stannis and the Hound were not wearing their
helmets during the battle. At first glance

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:23.420
it might seem strange that George would complain
about such a small detail, but it actually

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:28.780
makes perfect sense. For him to later reveal
that Rhaegar never fought Robert on the Trident,

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:33.220
a big deal would obviously be made about one
member of the kingsguard wearing Rhaegar's

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:37.210
armor and helm. But those are just theories
and that's all we have until Game of Thrones

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:42.040
prequel series, House of the Dragon, comes
out. Every question, doubt or proof we are

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:47.430
looking for will be answered or confirmed
in 2022 on HBO. Thank you so much for watching,

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:51.050
if you enjoyed this video make sure to give
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in

